/P 88 0 R
/E (From an institutional perspective, Josephine Kayere Njuguna highlighted the role of Technical and Vocational Education and Training \(TVET\) in embedding sustainability into curricula. Discussions emphasised the need for education systems, particularly in sectors such as hospitality, to prepare young women for climate-related disruptions, while also fostering socially responsible and environmentally conscious professionals.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (The panel also examined the need for systemic shifts within education systems to ensure that women are not only technically competent but also equipped with the mindset and awareness required to engage with sustainability challenges.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
