/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (Moreover, the inclusion of township-focused perspectives contributed to a more comprehensive understanding of the continuum between rural, peri-urban, and urban informal settings. These contexts are often interconnected through patterns of migration, economic exchange, and social networks, particularly in the Global South. As such, development strategies aimed at empowering women must take into account these linkages to ensure coherence and sustainability. Lessons drawn from township-based initiatives, including collective savings mechanisms, mentorship programmes, and micro-enterprise development, offer valuable points of reference for rural development efforts.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
368 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (In this regard, the participation of Etsoseng Foundation reinforced the importance of cross-context collaboration and knowledge exchange. It highlighted the need to move beyond rigid geographic categorizations and instead adopt inclusive approaches that recognize the shared challenges and opportunities facing women across different but interconnected environments. This contribution strengthened the overall discourse of the conference and supported its objective of advancing integrated, women-led development pathways towards 2030.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
